{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "That's Christmas To Me connects directly to my repeated Christmas listening, and its vocal holiday sound makes it the one I would try.",
    "Christmas At Downton Abbey also fits the holiday theme I have returned to, even though I would choose only one album this visit."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "A rock retrospective or singer-songwriter album does not satisfy the holiday listening interest behind my choice, even if I might enjoy it another time.",
    "Titles such as Partners and 16 Most Requested Songs give me too little connection to my listening history to make me want to try them."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The choices seem to assume that an interest in a few albums means I am looking broadly for familiar vocal music.",
    "Precious Memories: Vol. II seems to stretch my interest in Christmas music into an interest in devotional listening, which is not what I want right now."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "Several of my past choices explicitly centered on Christmas; that shared purpose matters more to me here than a broad musical resemblance.",
    "I rarely choose something without a clear reason, so a loosely related album is unlikely to interest me enough to act."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly recognize my holiday listening interest but extend it too broadly into albums that do not give me the same reason to listen."
}"}
